  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line a large oven tray with baking paper. Thinly slice the onion. Cut the tomatoes into thin wedges. Discard the husk and silks from the corn, then slice the kernels from the cob. Coarsely grate the cheese.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/301554/photos/large/prep_ingredients-471810b4f605df190bb4ce0aa70d2648.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Caramelise onion: Heat 2 tsp olive oil in a small frypan over medium heat. Cook the onion, stirring regularly, for 6 mins or until softened. Add 2 tsp balsamic vinegar and 1 tsp sugar and cook, stirring, for 2 mins or until caramelised. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/301555/photos/large/caramelise_onion-545a2a8cb981bb1040261e4b6fd6acff.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake pizzas: Put 2 pita breads on the lined tray. Combine the Italian seasoning, 2 tbs tomato paste and 2 tsp olive oil in a bowl. Spread evenly over the pitas, then top with the caramelised onion, half the spinach, tomato and three-quarters of the corn. Scatter over the cheese. Bake the pizzas for 10-12 mins until golden and crisp.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/301556/photos/large/bake_pizzas-8919079e94eaa60706d0f4c098842b2b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make salad: Meanwhile, put the remaining spinach, remaining corn, 2 tsp olive oil and 2 tsp balsamic vinegar in a bowl, season with salt and pepper and toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/301557/photos/large/make_salad-a1d399956595e20dacdabf5686f261fa.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Cut the pizzas into wedges and divide among plates. Serve the salad on top or on the side. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/301558/photos/large/serve_up-54deff24ca631208f2242d40b83fb74d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: If you like a kick of heat, add a pinch of chilli flakes to the tomato paste mixture, or scatter over to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/301559/photos/large/make_it_spicy-d4082963a6223f95cc8940b2592cd1cd.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
